      "solution": "n, m = map(int, input().split())\nrow = [1]\nfor _ in range(n):\n    print(''.join('#' if v % m else '.' for v in row))\n    row = [1] + [(row[j] + row[j+1]) % m for j in range(len(row) - 1)] + [1]",
      "statement": "Build the first [[N]] rows of Pascal's triangle: each row starts and ends with 1, and every other number is the sum of the two numbers just above it.\n\n    1\n    1 1\n    1 2 1\n    1 3 3 1\n\nNow replace every number by a single character:\n- {{#}} if the number is NOT divisible by [[M]]\n- {{.}} if the number IS divisible by [[M]]\n\nPrint the result, left-aligned, one row per line... and look closely at what appears.",
